  <text>
    <front>
      <div>
        <head>Disclaimer</head>
        <p>This customization is based on the <ref target="https://www.tei-c.org/Vault/P5/4.9.0/xml/tei/custom/odd/tei_odds.odd">TEI 4.9.0 release of the tei_odds.odd customization</ref> for authoring TEI ODDs and is being modified to accomodate the authoring of MEI ODD files.</p>
        <p>Aside from the overdue modernization of the MEI ODDs Schema, a major reason for updating to tei:4.9.0 was the introduction of <gi>constraintDecl</gi> which allows Schematron query language binding and schematron namespace declarations.</p><?TODO evaluate 4.10.0 and 4.11.0 ?>
      </div>
      <div xml:id="introduction">
        <head>Introduction</head>
        <p>The definitions of both the <expan>Music Encoding Initiative</expan> (<abbr>MEI</abbr>) Guidelines and the Schemata are facilitated in so called <expan>One-Document-Does-it-all</expan> (<abbr>ODD</abbr>) syntax as defined by the Text Encoding Initiative (TEI) XML dialect. Because the specifications of the TEI dialect emcompass a vast amount of elements and attributes for various kinds of text markup, creating a subset for the purposes of the MEI definitions is strongly adviseable. This <soCalled>customization</soCalled> is defined in the backmatter of this document. Moreover this document summarizes a set of editorial conventions for encoding the <term>MEI Guidelines</term> according th this schema.</p>
          <p>The editorial conventions aim to produce markup that is <term>parsimonious</term>, <term>semantic rather than presentational</term>, and aligned with concrete downstream behaviors (rendering, glossary generation, indexing, cross-referencing, validation).</p>
        <p>The guiding principle throughout: markup should earn its presence by enabling a behavior or capturing a distinction that matters. Tagging that does not achieve an effect is a cost without a benefit.</p>
      </div>
      <divGen type="toc" />
    </front>
    <body>
      <div xml:id="rollout-levels">
        <head>Encoding Levels and Rollout Plan</head>
        <p>The encoding conventions are organized in five cumulative <term>encoding levels</term>. Each level is a enrichment of the previous one and augments the encoding to facilitate specific output intentions.</p>
        <list type="ordered" style="list-style: none;">
          <item>
            <label>Level 1 — Consistent baseline encoding.</label>
            <gloss>Apply the mei_odds schema to ensure a consistent structural encoding of the MEI specifications (aka source and guidelines).</gloss>
          </item>
          <item>
            <label>Level 2 — Bibliography.</label>
            <gloss>Introduce <gi>bibl</gi> and related elements; build a coherent bibliography that examples and prose can reference.</gloss>
          </item>
          <item>
            <label>Level 3 — Musical works and their authors.</label>
            <gloss>Tag musical works mentioned or used as examples (<gi>title</gi>, <gi>persName</gi>, with appropriate<att>xml:lang</att>), supporting indexing.</gloss>
          </item>
          <item>
            <label>Level 4 – Semantic sugar.</label>
            <gloss>Introduce and settle core distinctions of: <gi>abbr</gi> vs. <gi>term</gi> vs. <gi>mentioned</gi> vs. <gi>name</gi>/<gi>orgName</gi>/<gi>persName</gi> vs. <gi>title</gi>) and apply them consistently. Decide explicitly what is <emph>not</emph> tagged.</gloss>
          </item>
          <item>
            <label>Level 5 — Cross-referencing apparatus.</label>
            <gloss>Introduce <gi>gloss</gi> and <gi>expan</gi> with <att>target</att>/<att>ref</att> attributes for index generation, mouseover behaviors, and a unified glossary.</gloss>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p><term>Encoding Level 1</term> should be achieved for <term>MEI 6.0</term>, all other levels are to be applied later and preferably step-by-step and consistently accross all MEI source files (docs nad modules) in the above order. The below encoding guidelines will illustrate the markup for <term>Encoding Level 1</term>, guidelines for the higher levels will be added when applicable.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Encoding Level 1</head>
        <p>The main goal of <term>Encoding Level 1</term> is consistency, including:<list>
          <item>File preamble</item>
          <item>Schema associations</item>
          <item>Metadata in the headers</item>
          <item>Markup of textstructures, e.g., <gi>div</gi> with <gi>head</gi> and <gi>p</gi></item>
          <item>Deprecation <att>rend</att> in favour of <att>rendition</att> or the TEI processing model</item>
          <item>Deprecation of <gi>abbr</gi> for lexicalized Latin discourse markers such as <q>e.g.</q> and <q>i.e.</q></item>
          <item><term>pureODD</term>-markup of specifications, e.g., <gi>elementSpec</gi></item>
          </list></p>
          <div>
            <head>Encoding Guidelines Chapters</head>
            <p>Each chapter of the guidelines is represented by one TEI document with <gi>TEI</gi> as root element. Consequently the file will contain <gi>teiHeader</gi> and <gi>text</gi> elements. While the header will be mostly identical in all chapters some metadata will be specific to the chapters:</p>
            <list type="gloss">
              <label>Analytic title</label>
              <item>
                <p>Encoded in <code lang="xpath">/TEI/fileDesc/titleStmt/title[level="a"]</code></p>
              </item>
              <label>Chapter editor</label>
              <item><p>Encoded in <code lang="xpath">/TEI/fileDesc/titleStmt/respStmt</code>, e.g.: <figure>
                <head>A chapter-specific responsibility statement</head>
                <teix:egXML xml:space="preserve"><respStmt>
  <resp>Edited by</resp>
  <name role="edt">Benjamin W. Bohl</name>
  <note>The editors listed here are responsible for the contents of this very chapter of the MEI Guidelines.</note>
</respStmt></teix:egXML>
                </figure></p> <p>The text of the chapter is to be encoded in <gi>body</gi> (<code>/TEI/text/body)</code>. Although <gi>front</gi>, and <gi>back</gi> are also available in <gi>text</gi>, their use is discouraged in chapters.</p> <p>The contents of the body have to start with a <gi>div</gi> holding a <att>xml:id</att> and a <gi>head</gi>, both of which hold the chapters heading. This should also be true for any subdivision of the chapter.</p></item>
            </list>
          <div>
            <head>Creating Element or Attribute Overview-Lists</head>
            <p>The MEI Guidelines contain overview lists of elements or attributes discussed or relevant in the respective section. These are encoded using the <gi>specList</gi> element with a child <gi>specDesc</gi> for each referenced element or attribute class. Attributes on the <gi>specDesc</gi> control, what to include, depending on the target type:<list type="gloss">
              <label>element</label>
              <item>add the value of the element’s <att>ident</att> into <att>key</att></item>
              <label>attribute(s)</label>
              <item>add the attribute classe’s <att>ident</att> into <att>key</att> and the <att>ident</att> values of all attributes from that class that you want to be listed as space-separated list into <att>atts</att>.</item>
              </list><figure>
              <head> Example-encoding of a element and attribute overview list</head>
              <teix:egXML><specList>
   <specDesc key="mdiv"/>
   <specDesc key="att.typed" atts="type"/>
   <specDesc key="att.classed" atts="class"/>
</specList></teix:egXML>
              </figure></p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <head>Encoding Code or Code References in the Textflow</head>
            <p>Every mention of any elements, attributes, models, or datatypes from the MEI specifications in the MEI Guidelines should be tagged following the below scheme, to facilitate automatic linking between the Guidelines and the Specifications.:<list type="gloss">
              <label>Mentioning element names</label>
              <item>
                <teix:egXML><gi scheme="MEI">note</gi></teix:egXML>
              </item>
              <label>Mentioning attribute names</label>
              <item>
                <teix:egXML><att>pname</att></teix:egXML>
              </item>
              <label>Giving examples for attribute values</label>
              <item>
                <p>Isolated attribute values in the text have to be marked using the <gi scheme="TEI">val</gi> element: <teix:egXML><val>c</val></teix:egXML></p>
                <p>For encoding an element with potential attributes definitions use <gi scheme="TEI">tag</gi>: <figure>
                  <head>Encoding and rendition of a <gi scheme="TEI">tag</gi> element.</head>
                  <teix:egXML><tag>note dur="4" oct="4" pname="c"</tag></teix:egXML>
                  <eg><tag>note dur="4" oct="4" pname="c"</tag></eg>
                  </figure></p>
              </item>
              </list></p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <head>Linking to other sections of the guidelines</head>
            <p>Two elements should serve this prupose: </p>
            <p><specList>
              <specDesc key="ptr"/>
              <specDesc key="ref"/>
              </specList></p>
          </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <head>Encoding Figures – Notation Examples and Codeblocks</head>
            <p>The Guidelines contain figures, such as notation examples from graphics files available in the repository, or generated on-build from MEI encodings with Verovio. Moreover, the code exmples can be rendered as codeblocks. Whichever you want to achieve, it must always be wrapped in a <gi>figure</gi> with a <gi>head</gi> encoding the figure caption (<?TODO ref/ptr ?> without any prefix or numbering; theses will be generated automatically).</p>
            <div>
            <head>Embedding a Graphics File</head>
            <p>To embed a graphics file use a <gi>graphic</gi> with <att>url</att>.</p>
            </div>
          <figure>
            <head>A <gi>graphic</gi> element referencing a pixelgraphic.</head>
            <teix:egXML><graphic url="../images/modules/usersymbols/triangle.png"/></teix:egXML>
          </figure>
            <div>
              <head>Rendering Codeblocks</head>
            <p>Codeblocks can be encoded using the <gi>eg:egXML</gi> element.</p>
            <figure>
              <head>Embedding a codeblock</head>
              <teix:egXML><figure>
                           <head>Accidentals encoded as <gi scheme="MEI">accid</gi> elements, independently from a <gi scheme="MEI">note</gi> element (instead of <att>accid</att>)</head>
                           <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" rend="verovio code" xml:space="preserve"><xi:include xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" href="../examples/verovio/accid-03.mei" parse="text"/></egXML>
                        </figure></teix:egXML>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <div>
            <head>Encoding Lists</head>
            <p>For encoding lists please refer to the TEI Guidelines <ref/>.</p>
          </div>
            <div>
            <head>Encoding Tables</head>
            <p>For encoding tables please refer to the TEI Guidelines <ref/>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
    <back>
      <div xml:id="documentation_structuralModifications">
        <head>Structural modifications</head>
        <p>A major structural modification to the definition of this customization is moving the <gi>schemaSpec</gi> to the <gi>back</gi> to free the <gi>body</gi> and make space for a documentation of this <term>ODD</term>. Although not required by TEI it, makes for a clearer separation of the two.</p>
        <p>Moreover, all the <gi>moduleRef</gi> elements have been moved into <gi>specGrp</gi> elements inside the respective sections in this documentation. This was done to facilitate accompanying the modification with some easier to read documentaiton and explanations. Theses definition now are included via <gi>specGrpRef</gi> elements into the <gi>schemaSpec</gi>.</p>
      </div>
      <div xml:id="documentation_schemaSpac">
        <head>Modifications to the schemaSpec</head>
        <specGrp xml:id="mod_element_schemaSpec">
          <?TODO enforce schemaSpec in back (?for customizations only?)?>
        </specGrp>
        <list rend="bulleted">
          <item><att>source</att> has been set to <val>tei:4.9.0</val>.</item>
          <item>The available <att>start</att> elements have been reduced to those used in the current MEI ODD files, i.e., <gi>TEI</gi> and <gi>specGrp</gi>.</item>
          <item>The <ident type="module">gaiji</ident> module has been excluded (for now).</item>
          <item>The <ident type="module">dictionaries</ident> module has been excluded.</item>
        </list>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Modification to the moduleRef elements</head>
        <p>As already describe in <ptr target="#documentation_structuralModifications" /> The <gi>moduleRef</gi> elements were moved due to major structural changes to the customization file.</p>
        <p>One of the most prominent changes to previous version of the MEI ODD schema is the drilled down inclusion of TEI modules and their respective elements. While there is a more detailed description of each module’s modifications below, there are some general principles that were applied:
        <list>
          <item>Only include elements currently used in MEI module definitions and guidelines</item>
          <item>Only include modules required due to elements, attribute classes or module classes they define</item>
        </list>
        </p>
        <p>Please be aware that the following does not list all modules defined by the TEI all ODD but just those, that are still included in the MEI ODD schema or had been included in the preceeding version.</p>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI header module</head>
          <p>The set of available elements has been reduced to:
          <list>
            <item><gi>availability</gi></item>
            <item><gi>change</gi></item>
            <item><gi>distributor</gi></item>
            <item><gi>edition</gi></item>
            <item><gi>editionStmt</gi></item>
            <item><gi>fileDesc</gi></item>
            <item><gi>license</gi></item>
            <item><gi>publicationStmt</gi></item>
            <item><gi>sourceDesc</gi></item>
            <item><gi>tagsDecl</gi></item>
            <item><gi>teiHeader</gi></item>
            <item><gi>titleStmt</gi></item>
          </list></p>
          <p>This reduces the allowed set of elements to those currently used in the headers of the source and guidelines files.</p>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_module_header">
            <moduleRef key="header" include="availability change distributor edition editionStmt fileDesc license publicationStmt sourceDesc tagsDecl teiHeader titleStmt"/>
            <classSpec module="header" type="atts" ident="att.citeStructurePart" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="header" type="atts" ident="att.patternReplacement" mode="delete" />
          </specGrp>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI core module</head>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_module_core">
            <moduleRef key="core" include="abbr desc emph foreign gloss graphic head hi item label list name note p ptr q quote ref resp respStmt term title"/>
            <classSpec module="core" type="atts" ident="att.milestoneUnit" mode="delete" />
          </specGrp>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI tei module</head>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_module_tei">
            
            <moduleRef key="tei"/>
            <?TODO mei-source.xml: edition back ?>
            <?TODO modules: seems to be all adequate errors ?>
            <?TODO drill down kept Attribute Classes ?>
            
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.anchoring" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.ascribed" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.breaking" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.cReferencing" mode="delete" />
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.canonical" mode="delete" />-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.citing" mode="delete" >
              <?TODO consider for later use ?>
            </classSpec>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.cmc" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.datable.w3c" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.datcat" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.declarable" mode="delete" />
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident=" att.declaring" mode="delete" />
            
  
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.docStatus" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.duration.w3c" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.editLike" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.edition" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.fragmentable" mode="delete"/>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.global.rendition" mode="delete">
              <!-\- keep to have @rend on e.g. egXML -\->
            </classSpec>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.global.responsibility" mode="delete"/>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.global.source" mode="delete"/>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.indentation" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.internetMedia" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.interpLike" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.measurement" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.naming" mode="change">
              <attList>
                <attDef ident="nymRef" mode="delete"/>
              </attList>
            </classSpec>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.notated" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.placement" mode="delete"/>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.pointing" mode="delete"/>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.ranging" mode="delete"/>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.resourced" mode="delete"/>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.scope" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.scoping" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.sortable" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.spanning" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.styleDef" mode="delete"/>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.typed" mode="delete"/>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.written" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.ascribed.directed" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.datable" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.dimensions" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.divLike" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" xml:id="GLOBAL" type="atts" ident="att.global" mode="change">
              <classes mode="change">
                <memberOf key="att.global.analytic" mode="delete"/>
                <memberOf key="att.global.change" mode="delete"/>
                <memberOf key="att.global.facs" mode="delete"/>
                <memberOf key="att.global.linking"/>
                
                <memberOf key="att.global.rendition"/>
                <memberOf key="att.global.responsibility" mode="delete"/>
              </classes>
            </classSpec>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.handFeatures" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.media" mode="delete">
              <?TODO there are two occurences each, of @widht and @height in the specs which I think don’t make sense?>
            </classSpec>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.naming" mode="delete">
              <!-\- keep to propagate att.canonical to tei:name -\->
            </classSpec>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.pointing.group" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.segLike" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.transcriptional" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.damaged" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.timed" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.formula" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.locatable" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.partials" mode="delete"/>
            <!--<classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.personal" mode="delete">
              <!-\- keep to propagate att.naming and att.personal to tei:name -\->
            </classSpec>-->
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.calendarSystem" mode="delete"/>
            <classSpec module="tei" type="atts" ident="att.duration.iso" mode="delete"/>
          </specGrp>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI gaiji module</head>
          <p>The module has been removed from the customization (for now).</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI textstructure module</head>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_module_textstructure">
            <moduleRef key="textstructure" include="TEI back body div text">
              <!-- N.B. doesn’t define Attribute Classes -->
            </moduleRef>
          </specGrp>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI tagdocs module</head>
          <p>As the members of this module are crucial for writing TEI ODD, it is the only module included without restrictions.</p>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_module_tagdocs">
            <moduleRef key="tagdocs" except="altIdent equiv model modelGrp modelSequence outputRendition param paramList paramspec">
              <!-- N.B. all Attribute Classe from tagdocs should be available when defining schemata with ODDs -->
            </moduleRef>
            
            <elementSpec ident="attDef" module="tagdocs" mode="change">
              <constraintSpec ident="attDefContents" scheme="schematron" xml:lang="en" mode="delete" />
            </elementSpec>
            
          </specGrp>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI dictionaries module</head>
          <p>The module has been removed from the customization.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI linking module</head>
          <p>No elements from this module are included, the sole resason for the module inclusion is its definition of <ident type="class">att.global.linking</ident>.</p>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_modules_linking">
            <moduleRef key="linking" include="" />
          </specGrp>
        </div>
        <div>
          <head>Modifications to the TEI figures module</head>
          <p>The elements allowed from this modules are <gi>cell</gi>, <gi>figDesc</gi>, <gi>figure</gi>, <gi>formula</gi>, <gi>row</gi>, and <gi>table</gi>. The only attribute class defined in this module (<ident type="class">att.tableDecoration</ident> has been removed for now, because so far, it is not being used in the MEI ODD files.</p>
          <specGrp xml:id="mod_module_figures">
            <moduleRef key="figures" include="cell figDesc figure formula row table">
              <!-- N.B. only defines Attribute Class att.tableDecoration which could make sense when writing guidelines -->
            </moduleRef>
            <classSpec ident="att.tableDecoration" module="figures" mode="delete" type="atts" />
          </specGrp>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>A new module: xinclude</head>
        <p>The <ident type="file">mei-source.xml</ident> file relies on XInclude to reference the individual ODD files of the MEI Guidelines chapters and module definitions. To facilitate the validation of <ident type="file">mei-source.xml</ident> even without active resolution of XInclude statements, the definition of the <gi scheme="xi">include</gi> element was borrowed from the <ref target="https://www.tei-c.org/Vault/P5/4.9.0/xml/tei/Exemplars/tei_xinclude.odd">TEI XInclude customization</ref> by the means of <soCalled>ODD chaining</soCalled>.</p>
        <specGrp xml:id="add_element_xi-include">
          <elementRef key="include" source="https://www.tei-c.org/Vault/P5/4.9.0/xml/tei/Exemplars/tei_xinclude.odd" />
        </specGrp>
        <p>Because a stray element without module assignment did not seem adequate a corresponding <ident type="module">xinclude</ident> module was added.</p>
        <specGrp xml:id="add_module_xinclude">
          <moduleSpec ident="xinclude">
            <desc xml:lang="en" versionDate="2026-05-08">Groups elements from the XInclude namespace.</desc>
          </moduleSpec>
          <specGrpRef target="#add_element_xi-include"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#mod_element_xi-include"/>
        </specGrp>
        <p>The <gi scheme="xi">include</gi> element then was modified (and this is where the actual <soCalled>ODD chaining</soCalled> happens), to be member of the <ident type="module">xinclude</ident> module. Moreover the definition of the <gi scheme="xi">include</gi> element was drilled down to what is actually in use in the MEI ODD files:
        <list>
          <item>available on the div-level, i.e., member of the <ident type="class">model.divLike</ident> to allow inclusion of the guidelines chapters</item>
          <item>available on the div-level, i.e., member of the <ident type="class">model.oddRef</ident> to allow inclusion of the module definitions</item>
          <item>no content, because MEI ODD files do not encode, e.g., a <gi scheme="xi">fallback</gi></item>
          <item>require the presence of a <att>href</att></item>
        </list></p>
        <specGrp xml:id="mod_element_xi-include">
          <elementSpec ident="include" ns="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" mode="change">
            <classes mode="replace">
              <memberOf key="model.divLike"/>
              <memberOf key="model.oddRef" />
            </classes>
            <content>
              <empty/>
            </content>
            <attList>
              <attDef ident="href" mode="change" usage="req" />
            </attList>
          </elementSpec>
        </specGrp>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Future Considerations</head>
        <p>The work on the MEI ODDs surfaced some ideas and future needs:
          <list>
            <item>Improve bibliographic references and citation by allowing<gi>bibl</gi>, <gi>cit</gi> from the core module</item>
            <item>Improve index generation by allowing <gi>divGen</gi> and adding some custom types to the XSLTs responsible for generating the guidelines</item>
            <item>Improve encoding of terms by allowing <gi>gloss</gi></item>
            <item>Improve referencing values from code examples by allowing <gi>mentioned</gi></item>
            <item>Improve citeability by adding and implementing <gi>citeStructure</gi></item>
            <item>Improve encoding of tables by adding <ident type="class">att.tableDecoration</ident> from the <ident type="module">gaiji</ident> module</item>
          </list>
          </p>
      </div>
      <schemaSpec ident="mei_odds" start="TEI specGrp" source="tei:4.9.0">

        <constraintDecl scheme="schematron">
          <sch:ns prefix="sch" uri="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron"/>
          <sch:ns prefix="sch1x" uri="http://www.ascc.net/xml/schematron"/>
        </constraintDecl>

        <moduleRef url="https://www.tei-c.org/release/xml/tei/Exemplars/relaxng.rng"/>
        
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_header"/>
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_core"/>
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_tei"/>
        <!--<moduleRef key="gaiji"/>-->
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_textstructure"/>
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_tagdocs"/>
        <!--<moduleRef key="dictionaries"/>-->
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_linking"/>
        <specGrpRef target="#mod_module_figures"/>
        <specGrpRef target="#add_module_xinclude"/>
        
      </schemaSpec>
    </back>
  </text>
</TEI>
